 # `fnox edit`
 
-- **Usage:** `fnox edit`
+- **Usage:** `fnox edit [KEY]`
 
-Edit the config file with secret values decrypted
+Edit the config file, or one secret, with values decrypted
 
-Decrypts or fetches every secret in the config file, across all profiles, into a private temporary copy and opens it in `$EDITOR` (then `$VISUAL`, then `vi`, or `notepad` on Windows). When the editor exits, fnox stores each new or changed value with its provider and writes the file back, keeping your comments and formatting. Unchanged values keep their existing ciphertext.
+Without KEY, decrypts or fetches every secret in the config file, across all profiles, into a private temporary copy and opens it in `$EDITOR` (then `$VISUAL`, then `vi`, or `notepad` on Windows). When the editor exits, fnox stores each new or changed value with its provider and writes the file back, keeping your comments and formatting. Unchanged values keep their existing ciphertext.
 
